@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour - Install the library and restyle it with tokens
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "Consuming developer" as dev
actor "Dashboard operator" as operator
box "Consumer - an installing application" #E0F2FE
  participant "Application shell" as app
end box
box "Library - src/qbc-grid" #ECFDF3
  participant "public-api.ts" as entry
  participant "GridComponent" as grid
  participant "grid.css" as styles
end box
box "Design system - qbc tokens" #D1FADF
  participant "qbc-tokens.css" as tokens
end box
box "Platform - desktop browser" #FFF4E5
  participant "DOM and compositor" as dom
end box

dev -> app : Install the package with Angular already present
app -> entry : Import GridComponent and GridTileTemplateDirective
note over entry, grid : Angular is a peer dependency, and no application package is referenced per L2-033
app -> grid : Render a grid with two tiles in edit mode
grid -> styles : Apply the component stylesheet
styles -> tokens : Read every colour, dimension, elevation, and duration per L2-034
tokens --> styles : Design-system defaults
styles -> dom : Paint the grid
dom --> operator : Present a draggable dashboard

dev -> app : Redefine --qbc-color-accent and --qbc-color-danger on a host element
app -> dom : Set the overriding custom properties
operator -> dom : Drag a tile
dom -> styles : Resolve the shadow fill
styles -> tokens : Read the overridden values, cascaded from the host
tokens --> styles : The application colours
styles -> dom : Paint the shadow in the application colours
dom --> operator : Present the restyled shadow, with no change to the library per L2-034

dev -> app : Open the route carrying the token file and the generated override sheet
app -> dom : Load both stylesheets before the first paint
operator -> dom : Drag a tile
styles -> tokens : Resolve every token the grid paints
tokens --> styles : The overriding values, each distinct from its default by construction
styles -> dom : Paint with the host's values, no library default surviving per L2-034
note over styles, dom : A hard-coded literal is precisely the value that would fail to move here

dev -> app : Open the route carrying no token file
app -> dom : Load the grid with its fallbacks alone
operator -> dom : Drag a tile
styles -> styles : Resolve each var() to the fallback beside it
styles -> dom : Paint, and the result matches the token-file render per L2-034
note over styles, dom : A fallback drifted from its token differs here, and in no other run
@enduml
